          <div id="historyList" class="history-list"></div>
        </article>

        <article class="panel claim-ledger">
          <span class="small-label">CLAIM LEDGER</span>
          <h2>What kind of statement is this?</h2>
          <div class="ledger-row">
            <strong>Symbolic</strong>
            <p>Date and number patterns create meaning, identity and routine structure. No medical causation is claimed.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="ledger-row">
            <strong>Personal</strong>
            <p>Your logs show what happened for you, under these conditions, at this point in time.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="ledger-row">
            <strong>Guideline</strong>
            <p>Public-health targets provide general context; they are not an individual diagnosis or prescription.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="ledger-row">
            <strong>Generated</strong>
            <p>The moment engine creates a suggestion from your inputs. You still choose whether, how or whether not to perform it.</p>
          </div>
        </article>
      </section>

      <section id="route" class="tab-panel">
        <article class="panel route-panel">
          <span class="small-label">FORMALISED ROUTE</span>
          <h2>From mental body to physical return</h2>
          <ol class="route-list">
            <li><strong>Moment:</strong> something happens in ordinary life.</li>
            <li><strong>Interpretation:</strong> SHIMS turns context and number-pattern into a small route.</li>
            <li><strong>Action:</strong> the person performs, adapts, swaps or declines.</li>
            <li><strong>Receipt:</strong> the app records what actually happened.</li>
            <li><strong>Adaptation:</strong> later suggestions learn from capacity and response.</li>
            <li><strong>Coding bodies:</strong> the working specimen is reverse-engineered into native JM structures.</li>
            <li><strong>Product:</strong> app, game and paid method grow from repeated useful returns.</li>
          </ol>
          <div class="route-equation">LIFE EVENT → MICRO ROUTE → BODY ACTION → RECEIPT → ADAPTATION</div>
          <img src="assets/body-return-roadmap.svg" alt="BUILT ENOUGH: BODY RETURN formal route infographic" class="roadmap-image" />
        </article>
      </section>
    </main>

    <footer>
      <p>SHIMS BODY RETURN v0.2 · Local-first · Your data stays in this browser unless you export it.</p>
      <p class="safety">Stop if you feel pain, chest pain, dizziness, faintness or unusual shortness of breath. Seek appropriate medical help when needed.</p>
    </footer>
  </div>

  <dialog id="sessionDialog">
    <form method="dialog" id="sessionForm">
      <button class="dialog-close" value="cancel" aria-label="Close">×</button>
      <span class="small-label">SESSION RECEIPT</span>
      <h2>Record the return</h2>
      <label>
        <span>Effort felt (1–10)</span>
        <input id="rpe" type="range" min="1" max="10" value="6" oninput="rpeOutput.value = value" />
        <output id="rpeOutput">6</output>
      </label>
      <label>
        <span>Mood before (1–5)</span>
        <input id="moodBefore" type="number" min="1" max="5" value="3" required />
      </label>
      <label>
        <span>Mood after (1–5)</span>
        <input id="moodAfter" type="number" min="1" max="5" value="4" required />
      </label>
      <label class="check">
        <input id="painReported" type="checkbox" /> Pain or worrying symptoms occurred
      </label>
      <label>
        <span>Notes</span>
        <textarea id="sessionNotes" rows="4" placeholder="What worked? What resisted? What changed?"></textarea>
      </label>
      <button class="primary-button wide" value="default">Save session receipt</button>
    </form>
  </dialog>

  <dialog id="microDialog">
    <form method="dialog" id="microForm">
      <button class="dialog-close" value="cancel" aria-label="Close">×</button>
      <span class="small-label">MOMENT RECEIPT</span>
      <h2>That came back</h2>
      <p class="muted" id="microReceiptSummary"></p>
      <label>
        <span>How did it feel? (1–5)</span>
        <input id="microEase" type="range" min="1" max="5" value="3" oninput="microEaseOutput.value = value" />
        <output id="microEaseOutput">3</output>
      </label>
      <label>
        <span>Mood after (1–5)</span>
        <input id="microMoodAfter" type="number" min="1" max="5" value="4" required />
      </label>
      <label class="check">
        <input id="microPainReported" type="checkbox" /> Pain or worrying symptoms occurred
      </label>
      <label>
        <span>Optional note</span>
        <textarea id="microNotes" rows="3" placeholder="Fast, awkward, energising, resisted, easier than expected…"></textarea>
      </label>
      <button class="primary-button wide" value="default">Save moment return</button>
    </form>
  </dialog>

  <script src="app.js"></script>
</body>
</html>
